  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "4ff33253-f45f-449c-8291-33c563e32bbb",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# stupid-\u0060for\u0060-loop tricks: finding repeating substrings\n\nIs your string made up of repeating substrings?"
    },
    {
      "id": "76fd5121-b7a6-4d75-9907-f930ce2ed2c2",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## testing for repeating substring"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2002590-577d-4309-a03d-89cc13ed8ea5",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "public static bool IsRepeatedSubstringPattern(string s) {\n    int n = s.Length;\n    \n    // The largest possible repeating substring length is n / 2\n    for (int len = 1; len \u003C= n / 2; len\u002B\u002B) {\n        if (n % len == 0) { // Substring must divide evenly\n            int left = 0;\n            int right = len;\n            bool match = true;\n\n            // Two pointers verifying segments match the prefix\n            while (right \u003C n) {\n                if (s[left] != s[right]) {\n                    match = false;\n                    break;\n                }\n                left\u002B\u002B;\n                right\u002B\u002B;\n            }\n\n            if (match) return true;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return false;\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "bd6e3107-2812-44b9-9117-dfdabd102970",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "IsRepeatedSubstringPattern(\u0022ABABAB\u0022)",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "True"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2c7434af-44c6-46da-b36c-a3f449e99547",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "IsRepeatedSubstringPattern(\u0022AAAAAB\u0022)",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "False"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7335a715-3080-4c9e-8224-ac113b47144d",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "IsRepeatedSubstringPattern(\u0022AAA\u0022)",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "mimeType": "text/plain",
          "content": "True"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "23c34ee1-d94e-4441-acf3-5095f39aa4bc",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## getting the repeating substring"
    },
    {
      "id": "ea25c6da-13cb-49b4-a215-77899d32e826",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "public static (string? substring, int count) GetRepeatingSubstringResult(string s)\n{\n    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(s)) return default;\n\n    int inputLength = s.Length;\n    bool isIterationLessThanOrEqualHalfInputLength(int i) =\u003E i \u003C= inputLength / 2;\n    bool isIterationMultipleInputLength(int i) =\u003E inputLength % i == 0;\n\n    for (int i = 1; isIterationLessThanOrEqualHalfInputLength(i); i\u002B\u002B)\n    {\n        if (!isIterationMultipleInputLength(i)) continue;\n\n        string candidate = s.Substring(0, i);\n\n        if(!IsCandidateConcatenatedEqualToOriginalInput(s, candidate, inputLength, i)) continue;\n        \n        return (candidate, inputLength / i);\n    }\n\n    return default;\n}\n\npublic static bool IsCandidateConcatenatedEqualToOriginalInput(string input, string candidate, int inputLength, int i)\n{\n    int repeatCount = inputLength / i;\n\n    string concatenated = string.Concat(Enumerable.Repeat(candidate, repeatCount));\n    \n    return (concatenated == input);\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "704b2daf-42d5-4057-aa97-ca7cdb44b33a",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "GetRepeatingSubstringResult(\u0022ABCABCABC\u0022)",
      "outputs": [
